<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_Warcasket_Siegebreaker (VFEPirates.WarcasketDef,
    ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase") at VFEP commit e237aba,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml. Everything not listed under "Tuning" below is
    still a verbatim Siegebreaker copy (placeholder, per TODOs.md), the VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets
    research prereq included.

    Tuning. VFEP reference numbers are the 10th-generation sets (Siegebreaker, Guardian,
    Controller, Sarcophagus, Brute) at the commit above. The set is a close-combat suit and is
    pitched at Brute and Guardian effectiveness, priced a little under them:
    - ArmorRating_Blunt 1.5 (Brute and Guardian; the other three 1.0): the close-combat plating,
      carried by all three pieces so the set reads as one tier, the Guardian pattern. Sharp 2
      and Heat 1 are the shared spacer values.
    - EnergyShieldEnergyMax 2.5 (Siegebreaker 2.5; Guardian, Controller and Sarcophagus 1.5;
      Brute 5.0): the bubble blocks ranged fire only, exactly what a melee suit needs while
      closing. EnergyShieldRechargeRate stays at the shared 0.01.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 6 / Plasteel 180 / Uranium 50 (Siegebreaker 6 / 145 / 50,
      Guardian 6 / 200 / 50). VFEP uses the spacer-component count as a tech-complexity dial
      (Controller 12 for mech control, the utility sets 6, Brute 4); a fuel-burning drop
      thruster is Aerial-tier tech, so 6 fits the utility-set tier and the plating step is
      priced onto plasteel instead. At vanilla market values (plasteel 9, spacer component 200,
      uranium 6) the full set welds for about 4690 silver without Odyssey: Siegebreaker 4195,
      Sarcophagus 4785, Guardian 5164, Brute 5220. The shoulders and helmet scale with the armor
      at the ratios the 10th-gen sets use between their pieces; see their headers for the
      arithmetic.

    SOS2/Universum parity: VFEP's 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml matches its own warcasket
    armor/helmet defs by an explicit defName list, so it never reaches this mod's defs. Our
    1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml applies the same EVA tag and Insulation_Cold override to this def
    and the helmet; see its header.

    Vanilla Gravship Expanded parity: VGE1's ArmorVacuumResistancePatch.xml lowers the five VFEP
    spacer warcasket armors to VacuumResistance 0.22 (helmets 0.65) by defName, so a full set
    needs an oxygen source; it never reaches this def. Our
    1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml (gated on VGE1's package id in
    LoadFolders.xml) applies the same 0.22 here; see its header. Without VGE1 the 0.2 below
    stands.

    Abilities: the armor is the drop engine.
    - Breach Jump: VEF CompAbilitiesApparel grants SCWC_BreachJump (rules and numbers in
      1.6/Defs/AbilityDefs/BreachJump.xml and Source/1.6/Abilities/), fuelled by the
      CompApparelReloadable beside it (100 charges of chemfuel at 1 per charge, 60-tick reload,
      20 per jump; Aerial's tank). The ability reads the tank off the apparel that holds it, so
      both comps must sit on this one def, which is why the engine is here and not on the
      shoulders as on Aerial.
    - SCWC_BreachJumpRange +20: the set's whole planet-side range (the shoulders and helmet add
      none; Aerial's full set reaches 40). In space the jump has no range limit and requires
      line of sight instead.
    - Space walking and the astrofuel swap under Vanilla Gravship Expanded come from
      1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/; stock Odyssey space terrain is impassable, so
      the main tree carries neither.
    - costList GravlitePanel 30 under Odyssey (MayRequire on the cost item, as Core's
      Buildings_Exotic.xml does for ShuttleEngine): the drop thrusters are gravtech. The
      shoulders and helmet take 10 each; the armor's larger 30 reflects that the thrusters and
      the unlimited-range space flight are its (cf. VGE2's combat vacsuit 20/10 split). A panel
      is market value 4 but costs 1 plasteel, 5 vacstone blocks and 1800 work (Odyssey's
      Items_Resource_Misc.xml), and vacstone only comes from space, so the 50-panel set total is
      the Odyssey premium: a been-to-orbit gate rather than a silver one, which is why the extra
      space functionality is priced here and not in the base costList.

    apparel tags: WarcasketVeteran is on every veteran-tier raid pawnkind of both VFEP
    factions plus Odyssey's VFEP_Salvager_Warcasket, so it is left commented out below per
    TODOs.md's acquisition question. WarcasketAll is only VFEP_General, the faction leader.

    Art: Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker (+
    _north/_east/_south), 256x256 RGBA under the root Textures/ folder, mirroring VFEP's own
    warcasket layout.

    apparel.renderNodeProperties adds the thruster-glow render node: the desaturated
    WarcasketShipcrackerThrusterGlow overlays (same canvas and facings as the armor art) drawn
    over the worn texture at an alpha that follows the Breach Jump's cast and flight
    (Source/1.6/Rendering/, thrusterGlowCurve in AbilityDefs/BreachJump.xml). color is the tint
    the grey art is multiplied by: chemfuel orange, between the yellow-white core and orange
    fringe of the VFEP_JumpFlame flecks it feeds; the Vanilla Gravship Expanded root's
    Patches/BreachJumpAstrofuel.xml swaps it to astrofuel purple, so the art must stay
    desaturated. TransparentPostLight draws after the light pass so the glow reads at night.
    parentTagDef ApparelBody puts the node beside the armor's own; baseLayer is only the
    fallback for a tree where that node is absent.

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own
    VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension and def inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves
    with two. VEF merges duplicate IMergeable extensions in a Def.ResolveReferences prefix,
    sorted by priority, first survives, the rest merge into it, and ApparelExtension.Merge does
    not copy moveSpeedFactorByTerrainTag. With equal priorities the parent's copy wins and the
    Vanilla Gravship Expanded space-walking factor is silently dropped; at priority 1 ours
    survives and every field of ours, from any load root, is kept. The helmet and shoulders
    carry the same guard.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Placeholder shipcracker warcasket shell. Stats are an untuned copy of the siegebreaker warcasket for now.</shortDescription>
    <description>Placeholder description for the shipcracker warcasket shell. It is a stand-in for later tuning, not lore.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>50</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>80</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>80</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
      <EnergyShieldRechargeRate>0.01</EnergyShieldRechargeRate>
      <EnergyShieldEnergyMax>2.5</EnergyShieldEnergyMax>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2</VacuumResistance>
      <SCWC_BreachJumpRange>20</SCWC_BreachJumpRange>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>6</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>180</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">30</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcracker</wornGraphicPath>
      <renderNodeProperties>
        <li>
          <debugLabel>SCWC_ThrusterGlow</debugLabel>
          <nodeClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.PawnRenderNode_ThrusterGlow</nodeClass>
          <workerClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.PawnRenderNodeWorker_ThrusterGlow</workerClass>
          <parentTagDef>ApparelBody</parentTagDef>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerThrusterGlow</texPath>
          <shaderTypeDef>TransparentPostLight</shaderTypeDef>
          <color>(1, 0.72, 0.38)</color>
          <baseLayer>31</baseLayer>
        </li>
      </renderNodeProperties>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <!-- Reusing WarcasketVeteran puts this set on every Junker/Mercenary
             veteran-tier pawnkind (and Odyssey's salvager pawnkind); see
             TODOs.md open question.
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        -->
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_ApparelReloadable">
        <maxCharges>100</maxCharges>
        <ammoDef>Chemfuel</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <hotKey>Misc4</hotKey>
        <chargeNoun>fuel</chargeNoun>
        <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>false</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>SCWC_BreachJump</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.CompProperties_ShieldBubble">
        <compClass>VEF.Apparels.CompShieldBubble</compClass>
        <blockRangedAttack>true</blockRangedAttack>
        <blockMeleeAttack>false</blockMeleeAttack>
        <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
        <showOnHostiles>true</showOnHostiles>
        <showOnNeutralInCombat>true</showOnNeutralInCombat>
        <shieldTexPath>Other/ShieldBubble</shieldTexPath>
        <chargeFullyWhenMade>true</chargeFullyWhenMade>
        <minShieldSize>2.1</minShieldSize>
        <maxShieldSize>2.7</maxShieldSize>
        <disableRotation>true</disableRotation>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>VFEP_WarcasketTrait</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
